"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[24926],{24926:function(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"content":"\\n<center>\\n<BookCard \\n          cover=\\"/assets/snippets/books/white-night-journey.png\\"\\n          title=\\"Journey Under the Midnight Sun\\"\\n          author=\\"Keigo Higashino\\"\\n          publisher=\\"Jaein\\"\\n          publishedDate=\\"2023-03-02\\"\\n          isbn=\\"9788990982612\\"\\n          rating=4\\n          tags=\\"thriller\\"\\n        />\\n</center>\\n\\n## Review\\nIn the final scene, Yukiho\'s last appearance, not batting an eye, conveys both shock and sadness.  \\nIt would be an expression of her cruelty and a final struggle to hide the sadness of losing her <mark>only sun</mark>.  \\nIt must be a famous scene that is ```terrible and dark``` yet desperately beautiful.  \\n<br>\\nTheir relationship is too bizarre and desperate to be called love, and it deeply explores the complex and dark abyss of human existence beyond a simple distinction between good and evil.  \\n<br>\\nThe psychology of the protagonists in the work is not directly narrated, so one must follow the story carefully.  \\n<br>\\nIn fact, it\'s difficult to fully empathize with their story and actions.  \\n<br>\\nIt leaves a deep lingering impression that makes the heart ache for a long time.  "}')}}]);